1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,400
When natural disasters strike
<font color="#FFE600"><b>ANYWHERE IN THE WORLD</b></font>

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:06,800
emergency operations centers
<font color="#FF2020"><b>LOSE 45 MINUTES</b></font>

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,800
manually cross-referencing
<font color="#FFE600"><b>AERIAL DRONE FOOTAGE</b></font>

4
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:12,800
chaotic radio chatter
and static maps.

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,800
Worse, off-the-shelf vision models
<font color="#FF2020"><b>ROUTINELY HALLUCINATE</b></font>

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,400
safe evacuation routes straight through
<font color="#FF2020"><b>12 FEET OF FLOODWATER</b></font>!

7
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:23,500
<font color="#FFE600"><b>CRISISGRID</b></font> is an autonomous
multimodal triage and dispatch agent,

8
00:00:23,700 --> 00:00:27,200
built on <font color="#FFE600"><b>FIVE META FRONTIER MODELS</b></font>.

9
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:32,200
Neural models propose;
pure deterministic Python <font color="#00FF20"><b>MATHEMATICS DISPOSES</b></font>.

10
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,200
In one click, CrisisGrid launches
<font color="#FFE600"><b>9x PARALLEL SAM-3.1 CALLS</b></font>,

11
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:40,000
separating <font color="#00FF20"><b>PASSABLE INFRASTRUCTURE</b></font>
from <font color="#FF2020"><b>CRITICAL HAZARDS</b></font>

12
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:44,200
like floodwater, debris, and damaged buildings
<font color="#FFE600"><b>IN JUST 5 SECONDS</b></font>.

13
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,000
Simultaneously, <font color="#FFE600"><b>MUSE-VOICE-TRANSCRIBE-1.0</b></font>
processes responder radio audio,

14
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:52,200
decoding the field unit's <font color="#FF2020"><b>MAYDAY CALL</b></font>
directly into structured text

15
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:57,500
with <font color="#00FF20"><b>OVER 99% ACCURACY</b></font>.

16
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,200
Next, <font color="#FFE600"><b>MUSE-SPARK-1.3</b></font> fuses the radio call
with segmented aerial imagery

17
00:01:04,400 --> 00:01:08,500
to evaluate <font color="#FF2020"><b>DAMAGE SEVERITY</b></font>
and propose candidate corridors.

18
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:12,800
Spark proposes in <font color="#FFE600"><b>DASHED YELLOW</b></font>,
<font color="#FFE600"><b>UNVERIFIED BY DESIGN</b></font>.

19
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:17,200
When its route cuts across floodwater
past our strict <font color="#FF2020"><b>10% TOLERANCE</b></font>,

20
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:21,800
our <font color="#FFE600"><b>LIANG-BARSKY GEOMETRY ENGINE</b></font>
<font color="#FF2020"><b>INSTANTLY REJECTS IT WITH PROOF</b></font>,

21
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:26,500
forcing an autonomous <font color="#FFE600"><b>SELF-CORRECTION LOOP</b></font>
onto dry elevated asphalt.

22
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:31,500
<font color="#00FF20"><b>ZERO PERCENT HAZARD CONTACT</b></font>:
<font color="#00FF20"><b>CORRIDOR ONE VERIFIED</b></font>.

23
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:36,500
Only <font color="#00FF20"><b>MATHEMATICALLY VERIFIED</b></font> coordinates
reach <font color="#FFE600"><b>MUSE-WONDER-1.0</b></font>

24
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:40,500
for <font color="#FFE600"><b>HIGH-EFFORT TACTICAL DISPATCH</b></font>.

25
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:44,800
A strict Python guardrail <font color="#FF2020"><b>HOLDS ANY UNIT</b></font>
targeted at an unverified zone.

26
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:49,500
Wonder synthesizes a <font color="#FFE600"><b>5-UNIT ALLOCATION</b></font>:
<font color="#00FF20"><b>DRONES · RESCUE BOATS · MEDICAL</b></font>.

27
00:01:49,800 --> 00:01:54,200
Alongside, <font color="#FFE600"><b>MUSE-IMAGE-1.0</b></font> renders an official
<font color="#00FF20"><b>TACTICAL BRIEFING CARD</b></font>

28
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:59,000
generated strictly from <font color="#00FF20"><b>VERIFIED FACTS ONLY</b></font>,

29
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:05,500
and one click exports the complete
<font color="#00FF20"><b>FEMA INCIDENT ACTION PLAN</b></font>.

30
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:11,800
To handle cascading crises,
CrisisGrid streams <font color="#FFE600"><b>LIVE EARTHQUAKES</b></font>

31
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:16,000
directly from the <font color="#FFE600"><b>USGS SEISMIC FEED</b></font>.

32
00:02:16,200 --> 00:02:20,500
Dispatchers select real epicenters to query
<font color="#00FF20"><b>HOSPITALS & SHELTERS VIA OSM</b></font>.

33
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:25,000
Finally, our <font color="#FFE600"><b>CLEARANCE DELTA ENGINE</b></font>
monitors post-engineering scenes,

34
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:29,800
re-scanning <font color="#00FF20"><b>CLEARED BRIDGES</b></font>
and flipping their status from <font color="#FF2020"><b>BLOCKED</b></font> to <font color="#00FF20"><b>GREEN</b></font>

35
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:34,500
ONLY when physical geometry verifies safe passage.

36
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:37,800
<font color="#FFE600"><b>5 META FRONTIER MODELS</b></font>.

37
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,200
<font color="#FFE600"><b>1 API KEY</b></font>.

38
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,000
<font color="#00FF20"><b>ZERO UNVERIFIED GUESSES</b></font>.
